cuda-temp-lists: a fix to intel/llvm v7.1.1, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

The driver removes the files a temporary list or table names only when the list or table is registered
with that type.  For NVIDIA targets sycl-post-link's table is registered as bitcode and llvm-foreach's
lists as PTX and objects, so every link left each device image's split bitcode, PTX and cubin in TMPDIR
(22 GB of a tmpfs /tmp in a day of builds).  spir64 registers them as lists and leaves nothing.
